- Added an explicit 7-case legal/illegal control table covering duplicate start, idempotent stop, healthy callbacks, stale generations, and late callbacks while stopping, disconnected, or failed.
- Added configuration to the continuation-driven stop matrix, yielding 8 deterministic stop/cancellation boundaries across every asynchronous startup step.
- Added all four mandatory-component health-loss cases and asserted capability revocation is published before cleanup starts.
- Added 32 concurrent starts (exactly one usable runtime), 32 repeated stop/health race generations, and existing 32-way duplicate-stop coverage.
- Replaced the fixture's aggregate resource count with separate task, timer, socket, channel, and dependency counters. One hundred factory lifecycle iterations restore all external counters and the coordinator's internal task/resource footprint after every generation.
- Replaced the continuous clock with a fixed fake clock. Correctness scheduling uses checked continuations only; the test file contains no sleep call or yield polling.

